# onTrack session (always-on)

Keep this file short on purpose. Load detail only when the task needs it.

## When to load more

| Task | Read |
|------|------|
| App UI / simulator / screenshot bug | `.cursor/skills/agent-ui/SKILL.md` **before** verify |
| Design / polish / “make it cool” | `~/.cursor/skills/think-cool/SKILL.md` |
| Cleanup / “optimize” | `~/.cursor/skills/optimize-code/SKILL.md` |
| Domain feature work | `.cursor/skills/<domain>/` (travel, todos, workouts, …) + `AGENTS.md` feature table |
| Form field icons / numeric inputs / migrations | matching `.cursor/rules/*` via globs |

## Non-negotiables (every session)

- **No personal identifiers** in source — see `no-personal-identifiers.mdc`.
- **App-affecting JS/UI** → `./scripts/agent-ui-verify-both.sh --route … [--flow <name>] --exists …` (named flow when not already on route). Assert/`--color` then stop. Docs/rules/host-only → skip simulator.
- **Headless verify** → agent UI runs on a dedicated headless pool device (`onTrack Agent N` / `onTrack_Agent_N`, up to 5 parallel; wait if full). Never open Simulator.app / emulator GUI unless the user explicitly asks (“headed”, “open Simulator”, “with window”). See agent-ui skill.
- **Dev Mode** → off by default. Seeds/flows may turn it on for mock data; `verify-both` / `agent-ui.sh devmode release` turn agent sandboxes off again. Do not leave it on.
- **Glyph / icon orientation** → fix from source (`Symbol`, `design-system/icons.ts`, platform maps, transforms). Never screenshot→vision loops for micro-glyphs; do not force-reconnect to “re-check” icons.
- **New/edited interactive controls** → `ontrack.*` `testID` + `ids.ts` + `docs/agent-ui-map.md` in the same change.
- **Dump = debt** → ≤1 dump to discover; same turn stamp id/map and/or named flow so that dump is never needed again (agent-ui skill).
- **Metro** → `npm run packager:ensure:start` (never `npm start` in agent shells). Prefer Fast Refresh; do not kill Metro / `--clear` / force-stop / `--force-reconnect` after routine edits. Node 24.
- **Stuck / slow / device timeout** → stop grinding. Classify the timeout, check health/pins once, then fix the cause (config/env/device pin / wedge / iOS system sheet / flaky wait) so it does not recur — see `stuck-check-config.mdc`.
- **Locality** → smallest entry file first; extract if touched file would stay >700 lines; prefer Shared patterns in `AGENTS.md`.
- **Responsive chrome** → `useResponsive()` + `AppText fit` (see `responsive-layout.mdc`).
- **Think cool** → UI should feel crafted/delightful (presence, one idea, restraint); for design/polish read `~/.cursor/skills/think-cool/SKILL.md`.
- **Smooth transitions** → continuous / eased motion over abrupt snaps; never break functionality or fluidity (Development `.cursor/rules/smooth-transitions.mdc`).
- **Optimize** → cleanup/rename/reuse/token-slim/temp removal; read `~/.cursor/skills/optimize-code/SKILL.md`.
- **`push`** → always `npm run ship:push -- -m "<concise why>"` (`scripts/ship-push.sh`). Same for “push script” / “ship push”. Flow: patch-bump `.xx` + release notes/changelog → commit → branch → PR → merge main → delete branch → TestFlight + device OTA (no APK). Do **not** treat bare `push` as plain git push. Use `--ota-only` to reship current main (no bump); `--skip-ota` to skip EAS Update. Native / `runtimeVersion` binary → `android:release-to-drive` / `build:device:android` separately.
